# General rules

- Write all code, comments, and commit messages in English.
- Mobile-first, responsive layout: phone, tablet, and desktop from a
  single codebase, no separate native app. Test any UI or navigation
  change on a real phone browser, not only desktop — don't wait until the
  end of the project to find out something breaks on a smaller screen.
- Keep changes narrowly scoped to what was asked. Never refactor or
  "clean up" adjacent components that weren't part of the request.
- Before considering a task done, re-run the full test suite, not just
  the tests near the file you touched.
- Never state a task is complete without concrete proof (a screenshot on
  the actual breakpoints affected, console output, or a passing test run
  pasted in full) — a status summary alone is not proof.
